<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andarax</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Andarax is a river in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, flowing from the Sierra <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alpujarras">Alpujarras</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> at the city of Almería. Its lower valley, irrigated since Roman and Islamic times, was the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechina">Pechina</a> (Bajjana), a leading port town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> in the 9th and 10th centuries. The river is dry for much of the year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andarax.jpg" alt="Andarax" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DescriptionAndarax.png This map was created from OpenStreetMap project data, collected by the community. … · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andarax.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
